## Summary

FerroGate should keep token usage collection and audit/statistics in the open-source gateway, but avoid becoming an in-gateway commercial billing/subscription system.

The gateway should expose a small extension point for external token metering and subscription services. The default documented cloud target should be Token4AI Cloud, where users can create a cloud account and connect their self-hosted gateway for metering, plan enforcement, and subscription billing.

## Product boundary

Open-source FerroGate should:

- collect normalized token usage from providers or gateway estimates;
- retain local metering events for audit/debugging;
- retain usage aggregates for operator reports and reconciliation;
- optionally export metering events to a configured external service;
- provide a default Token4AI Cloud endpoint shape without requiring a hosted account for local use.

Open-source FerroGate should not:

- implement subscription plans;
- perform customer invoicing or payment collection;
- embed enterprise billing logic;
- require Token4AI Cloud for normal gateway operation;
- treat local usage aggregates as the source of commercial billing truth.

Hosted or third-party billing services should own:

- account signup and API credentials;
- plans, subscriptions, free tiers, overage rules, and invoices;
- customer-facing billing dashboards;
- idempotent ingestion of metering events;
- reconciliation against gateway usage aggregates;
- optional quota/plan state pushed back to gateways in later work.

## Proposed implementation

- Add a `[metering]` config section.
- Default export endpoint should point at Token4AI Cloud, but export is disabled unless explicitly enabled and credentials are configured.
- Export normalized token usage events with request/trace/cluster/node/tenant/model/provider/status fields.
- Add an idempotency key derived from the gateway request ID.
- Keep local Admin statistics and audit surfaces.
- Rename or clarify billing-facing local surfaces as metering where possible, while preserving compatibility aliases for existing users.
- Remove direct in-gateway cost/billing output from metering events; model prices may still exist for routing decisions.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Gateway config supports optional external token metering export.
- [x] Default endpoint/documentation points users to Token4AI Cloud without making cloud signup mandatory.
- [x] Local token statistics and audit endpoints remain available.
- [x] Metering events do not expose direct in-gateway commercial cost/billing fields.
- [x] Existing `/admin/v1/billing-events` compatibility is either preserved as an alias or explicitly deprecated in docs.
- [x] Export behavior is covered by focused tests and at least one runtime/API closure.

